Permission for the official builds (DRAFT: this text is to be reviewed by a
lawyer before the next release tag)

The author permits, free of charge and without asking, the use of the logo
as part of the StokesForge software **when that software is unmodified**:

1. in the official packages published by the author (archives, installers, RPM
   and DEB packages): as the icon of the application, of its window, of its
   executable and of its project files, and in its About window;
2. in a build that anyone makes from the unmodified source of an official
   release, with the logo files left as published.

Nothing else is permitted. In particular:

- the logo may not be modified (cropped, recoloured, redrawn, animated, or
  used as the basis of another drawing);
- the logo may not be used outside this software: not in another project, not
  in an extension or plug-in for StokesForge, not in a derived product, not as
  the mark of a service or of a company;
- a modified version of StokesForge (its code modified in any way) removes the
  logo from its builds and packages: the permission above does not extend to
  it. The code builds and runs without this directory, and it is not needed to
  use or modify the code.

The name StokesForge and the logo are excluded from the licence of the code:
under section 7(e) of the GNU GPL version 3, the GPL grants no right to use
them as trade names, trademarks or service marks. This permission grants no
trademark right either.

The code of StokesForge stays under GPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSE at the root of
the repository); this notice takes nothing from it. Apart from the permission
above, a distribution of the code, modified or not, leaves this directory out
unless the author has given written permission. The official packages carry this
notice as licenses/logo/LICENSE.
